On Sat, Oct 23, 2010 at 20:53, Lindar <lindarthebard@yahoo.com> wrote:
> Wouldn't it be better to have some sort of website or somesuch so we
> can have pictures like a newspaper? I think it would be fun to do
> that. We could also have a personal interests section and a 'fun
> activities in Lojbanistan' portion. Maybe bring up all the different
> networking platforms we have?

Yea it seems to me that there's probably another tool/site that can be used
to make this much more efficient. Btw, I just tried editing the Google
document, and I didn't have the proper permissions.

1) If the idea is just to aggregate news for/by lojbanists

   - Editing: we could use status.net (or closed-source twitter), and then
   - Reading: aggregate all the feeds on a webpage (some code required)

2) But this sounds really similar to just starting multi-user blog, i.e.
blogger, wordpress etc.

   - Editing: people request to be added as authors, authors could edit one
   another's text
   - Viewing: just visit the prepackaged URL

3) Or if we want to appear like a social network, we could use any of Ning
(closed source), grou.ps (open) or buddypress (open) for a
no-coding-necessary "social network in a box."

4) OR! (wait for it) ...Just use the tiki!

I think it would be cool to try out one of the social networky options
listed in 3) above --particularly the open source ones. If anyone else
shares the interest, it might be fun to try a 'jefnuz' out on each one out
and review them as a group.

co'o mi'e korbi

